\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces $F_1$ at two blow-up sizes. (a) $\alpha =0.2$: the only point where the leading terms balance is the barycentre, which carries the positive critical point; a real critical point with $y_1<0$ sits over $(\alpha ,1-2\alpha )$, outside the positive theory. (b) $\alpha =0.6$: the leading terms balance along an open segment, whose endpoints (open circles) have no positive balance, and the critical points all sit over one point of it. (c) $\alpha =0.6$: the $u_1$-marginal of the thimble law with $\hbar =T^h$ (\cref  {thm:tropical,ex:levels}). At $h=0$ it is the marginal of the uniform law on $Q$; at $h=h^*=0.2$ it is uniform on the segment; at $h=0.3$ it is uniform on $[0.3,0.5]$; above $0.4$ it is concentrated at $u_1^*=0.4$. Here $\log T=-200$, and $-100$ for $h=0.45$.}}{15}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:F1}{{1}{15}{$F_1$ at two blow-up sizes. (a) $\alpha =0.2$: the only point where the leading terms balance is the barycentre, which carries the positive critical point; a real critical point with $y_1<0$ sits over $(\alpha ,1-2\alpha )$, outside the positive theory. (b) $\alpha =0.6$: the leading terms balance along an open segment, whose endpoints (open circles) have no positive balance, and the critical points all sit over one point of it. (c) $\alpha =0.6$: the $u_1$-marginal of the thimble law with $\hbar =T^h$ (\cref {thm:tropical,ex:levels}). At $h=0$ it is the marginal of the uniform law on $Q$; at $h=h^*=0.2$ it is uniform on the segment; at $h=0.3$ it is uniform on $[0.3,0.5]$; above $0.4$ it is concentrated at $u_1^*=0.4$. Here $\log T=-200$, and $-100$ for $h=0.45$}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:F1@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][14][]15}}
