\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {26}{\ignorespaces What information is worth (\cref  {ex:voi}). (a) The fibre's shadow at $2400$ units on route B, cut by the threshold into laws favouring each action: the value of identification is twice the smaller overhang. (b) The value of identification along both routes: route A flips the decision with no value of information at all. (c) A signal about the unit along route B: Bayes under maximum entropy, the robust value with pure and with mixed policies, and the envelope of classical values over the fibre. (d) Information, identification and decision gains against the signal's accuracy. (e) The value of the signal and of identification against the threshold: largest at the decision boundary. (f) Dilation: observing $B_0$ can widen the interval of the never-observed quantity, though never on a rigid face.}}{76}{figure.26}\protected@file@percent }
