\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {31}{\ignorespaces The figure-eight pseudo-diagram (\cref  {prop:figeight}). (a) The $16$ resolutions, with rows for the signs of crossings $1,2$ and columns for crossings $3,4$; $3_1$ and $3_1^*$ are the right- and left-handed trefoils, $4_1$ the figure-eight and U the unknot. The knot is nontrivial exactly in the block where both twist regions agree. (b) For one law, the range of $P(\text  {knotted})$, $P(\text  {figure-eight})$ and the chirality allowed by five levels of data. Triples fix the chirality but not $P(\text  {knotted})$, which needs all four crossings together.}}{90}{figure.31}\protected@file@percent }
