\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {44}{\ignorespaces Every critical point of the three potentials, grouped by fibre, with its leading holonomies drawn as dials (the arrow is the phase of $y_j$). A and B have one fibre each. C has two: eight points over the leximin fibre and two over $(1/40,1/40,9/40)$. In each case the number of critical points equals the normalised volume of the Newton polytope, which equals $\chi $, and that equality certifies the list complete. For C these are the critical points of the uncorrected $W$ (\cref  {rem:corrections}).}}{144}{figure.44}\protected@file@percent }
